Not quite... items that give reflection or disintegration extrinsic
properties are not damaged by wide-angle beams.  Of course, that only
protects shields of reflection and silver and black dragon
scales/scale mail...

>From youprop.h:

#define EReflecting             u.uprops[REFLECTING].extrinsic

>From prop.h:

#       define W_ARM        0x00000001L /* Body armor */
#       define W_ARMC       0x00000002L /* Cloak */
#       define W_ARMH       0x00000004L /* Helmet/hat */
#       define W_ARMS       0x00000008L /* Shield */
...
#       define W_ARMU       0x00000040L /* Undershirt */

EReflecting will be 8 if you have a shield of reflection, 1 if you
have silver dragon scale(s| mail), or 9 with both.  EDisint_resistance
is similarly defined, and will be 1 with BDSM or similar scales.

>From pray.c:

            if (uarms && !(EReflecting & W_ARMS) &&
                        !(EDisint_resistance & W_ARMS))
                (void) destroy_arm(uarms);

Now, uarms is true if you are wearing a shield.  If you have
reflecting from any other method than being polymorphed into a silver
dragon (since there is no intrinsic reflection that may be gained by
eating something), you have extrinsic reflection, and thus EReflecting
is true (something non-zero).  W_ARMS is 8 (see include/prop.h), so if
your shield gives either extrinsic reflection or disintegration
resistance, the entire conditional becomes false and the item is not
destroyed.

The same thing happens for body armor.  Cloaks have similar code for
them, but no cloak currently gives either extrinsic, so they are
disintegrated.  All shirts are also destroyed (without the useless
checks for extrinsic protection).

Finally, you only avoid fry_by_god if you have Disint_resistance
(intrinsic or extrinsic).  Reflection does not prevent you getting
destroyed, but your nice shield of reflection or SDSM will be sitting
on top of your bones pile!

